AERA additions in source/src/cmd:
- --aera recovery integration mode with an exact, empty output directory.
- Machine-readable progress at 10 Hz, explicit partition selection and strict hashes.
- Safe partition names and bounded XZ/ZSTD decoder memory in recovery mode.
- ZSTD (REPLACE_ZSTD, operation 14) enabled in the verified direct writer.
- Disable terminal decoration/metadata scanning in recovery mode.
- Explicit --aera-block-fd direct-write phase using only an inherited block fd.
  Independently checks the reviewed manifest, extent coverage, bounded codecs and
  operation SHA-256; writes zero/discard extents explicitly. Does not create,
  truncate or unlink targets. AERA claims/resizes/unmounts targets and requires
  flushed block readback SHA-256 before reporting success; no slot activation.
  Direct flashing is an Advanced opt-in, not an update_engine replacement.

Only the offline feature set is built; no HTTP client is included.
The prebuilt is for Android/Bionic ARM64, API 28 or newer.
Other recovery architectures continue using the built-in extractor.
build.sh reproduces the binary from the included source and locked dependencies.
